Spring Boot:
Java framework for backend development.

Why Spring Boot:
- Easy setup
- Embedded server
- Fast development

Request Flow:
Client -> Controller -> Service -> Repository -> Database

REST API:
Used for communication between client and server.

HTTP Methods:
GET -> Fetch data
POST -> Create data
PUT -> Update data
DELETE -> Delete data

Data format: JSON

Spring Boot Structure:

src/main/java -> Java code
src/main/resources -> Config files
pom.xml -> Dependencies

Main class:
Contains @SpringBootApplication

Packages:
controller
service
repository
model
